        <h2>Local Insights & Solutions</h2>
        <div class="solution-content">
          <p><strong>Research Source:</strong> content_ideas_for_zanzibar.csv</p>
          <p><em>Based on NYT '36 Hours in Zanzibar, Tanzania' (2271 est. visits, 17 backlinks). Content enriched with local expertise from Dhow Coast Travels licensed guides.</em></p>

          <h3>Priority 1: Stone Town (Morning - 4 hours)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>House of Wonders & Palace Museum - UNESCO architecture</li>
            <li>Freddie Mercury House - iconic photo spot</li>
            <li>Darajani Market - spices, textiles, local life</li>
            <li>Forodhani Gardens - seafront walk</li>
            <li><strong>Dhow Coast tip:</strong> Licensed walking tour ($13-80) covers all highlights efficiently</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Priority 2: Spice Farm Experience (Afternoon - 3 hours)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Kidwaju or Kizimkazi spice farm - sensory walk</li>
            <li>Cloves, vanilla, cinnamon, nutmeg - touch, smell, taste</li>
            <li>Swahili lunch with farm-fresh ingredients</li>
            <li><strong>Dhow Coast tip:</strong> Combo tour with Prison Island saves transit time</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Priority 3: Sunset & Evening (3 hours)</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Sunset dhow cruise from Stone Town harbor</li>
            <li>Forodhani night market - grilled seafood, Zanzibar pizza</li>
            <li>Rooftop bar at Emerson on Hurumzi or Africa House</li>
            <li><strong>Dhow Coast tip:</strong> Book sunset cruise + dinner package for seamless evening</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>If You Have 48+ Hours: Add These</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Mnemba Atoll snorkeling (full day) - pristine coral, dolphins</li>
            <li>Prison Island - giant tortoises, snorkeling</li>
            <li>Jozani Forest - red colobus monkeys, mangrove walk</li>
            <li>Nungwi/Kendwa beaches - stay overnight for sunrise</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Logistics for Short Stays</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Airport → Stone Town: 15 min, pre-book transfer (TRF-01)</li>
            <li>Stone Town is walkable - no car needed for 36 hours</li>
            <li>Stay in Stone Town to maximize time, minimize transit</li>
            <li>WhatsApp us for real-time adjustments based on weather/tides</li>
          </ul>
